{"id": "De9jms9Doe7", "title": "Video by feartalkies", "description": "A woman stood weeping in the middle of a lake at midnight, and told a loyal guard his king would die in three days. 🌧️\n\nVikram & Betaal: Who Waits at the Gate?\n\nThe parts we couldn't fit in the reel:\n\nViravara came to King Shudraka with only his wife, his son, his daughter, a dagger, a sword and a shield, and asked for 500 gold coins a day. The king had him followed in secret. His spies found that he gave a hundred to his wife for food, spent a hundred on clothes, gave a hundred to worship and two hundred to the poor, and then guarded the palace gate alone, every night.\n\nThe weeping woman was the Earth herself, grieving for the good king she was about to lose.\n\nWhen the boy was offered, a voice from the sky praised Viravara: he had saved his king's life. Before she followed her children into the fire, his wife prayed to be his wife again in her next life.\n\nWhen they rose, Viravara woke as if from sleep and asked how they were alive. His family said only that the goddess had saved them. The next morning the king told his whole court what he had seen, and gave Viravara and his son two kingdoms, Lata and Karnata. The guard and the king lived as equals.\n\nSo, who was braver? The father who gave his son for his king, or the king who would give his own head for a servant? 👇\n\n#vikrambetaal #indianhorror #ghoststories #indianfolklore #halloween", "channel": "feartalkies", "uploader_id": "58803293522", "uploader": "Fear Talkies | Indian Horror", "timestamp": 1793026952, "like_count": 1596, "comment_count": 9, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-17970541754965523a", "ex